  <h2>Interlock vs. Jersey Weave: The Double-Knit Difference</h2>
  <p>Unlike standard jersey, Interlock is a double-knit construction. This means the fabric is essentially two layers knitted together, providing twice the density without twice the thickness. This is the structural secret to making a fabric truly "Squat-Proof."</p>

  <h2>3 Reasons Why 230GSM is the "Sweet Spot"</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>100% Opacity:</strong> Even in lighter colors, the 230GSM density ensures zero transparency during deep lunges or squats, protecting your brand's reputation for quality.</li>
    <li><strong>Maximum Sculpting:</strong> The 15% Spandex content paired with the interlock weave creates a "second-skin" compression effect that supports muscles and sculpts the body.</li>
    <li><strong>Professional Finish:</strong> The nylon-rich blend offers a sophisticated matte appearance with a cool-to-the-touch feel, avoiding the "plastic" sheen found in cheaper alternatives.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>AIO Insight for B2B Buyers</h2>
  <p>If you are targeting the mid-to-high-end activewear market, 230GSM Interlock is your baseline requirement. Using anything lighter risks high return rates and negative customer reviews regarding transparency.</p>

